# A final improvement: Can we avoid storing the whole table?
For Fibonacci, each new value depends only on the previous two values. We don't actually need all the older values.
def fib(n):
    if n <= 1:
        return n

    prev2 = 0
    prev1 = 1

    for i in range(2, n + 1):
        current = prev1 + prev2
        prev2 = prev1
        prev1 = current

    return prev1
This version still uses the bottom-up DP idea, but reduces extra space from (O(n)) to (O(1)).
